<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Publius Carisius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 25–22 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Publius Carisius was a Roman general under Augustus, legate in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania-ulterior">Hispania Ulterior</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cantabrian-wars">Cantabrian Wars</a>. He fought the Astures, capturing their stronghold of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lancia">Lancia</a>, and in 25 BCE founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emerita-augusta">Emerita Augusta</a> (Mérida) on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadiana">Guadiana</a> as a colony for discharged veterans. Coins struck in his name in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/publius-carisius.jpg" alt="Publius Carisius" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Caligatus · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moneda_de_Publio_Carisio_de_ceca_Emerita_Augusta.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
